  "goodToKnow": "Das Männchen is a male animal: Männchen und Weibchen. Literally, it's a little man, so it's also used for small figures: das Ampelmännchen, the little man on pedestrian lights. The East German Ampelmännchen with his hat was saved after reunification by public campaigns and is now a Berlin icon on T-shirts and mugs. Männchen machen means to sit up and beg, said of dogs, or to bow and scrape. Neuter, like all -chen words."
